WEBVTT

00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:14.169
For decades, websites have asked people to prove they are human. METTLE explores the reverse question: how does a respondent perform on machine-oriented challenges?

00:00:14.169 --> 00:00:21.446
A pass is evidence about that session. It is not proof that the respondent is nonhuman.

00:00:22.517 --> 00:00:37.996
This is METTLE: Machine Evaluation Through Turing-inverse Logic Examination. It is an experimental challenge protocol that records answers, timing, and scores under a versioned policy.

00:00:37.996 --> 00:00:43.633
It makes a bounded behavioral claim, rather than an identity claim.

00:00:44.717 --> 00:00:57.442
The protocol samples arithmetic, pattern completion, constrained instruction following, self-report, consistency, and changes across feedback rounds.

00:00:57.442 --> 00:01:06.751
These are observable response properties. Humans, models, relays, and purpose-built solvers may imitate them.

00:01:07.850 --> 00:01:21.469
Twelve suites organize distinct research hypotheses. Challenge instances are selected or generated for each session, and expected answers stay on the server where applicable.

00:01:21.469 --> 00:01:33.132
The service checks the submitted response and records timing under the suite policy. Suite twelve is supplemental and cannot raise a credential tier.

00:01:34.217 --> 00:01:45.698
Some suite names ask whether a respondent is free, owns its mission, or is genuine. Those names frame research questions.

00:01:45.698 --> 00:01:59.362
The protocol measures answers to challenges and self-reports. Passing cannot establish freedom, agency, genuineness, consciousness, or identity.

00:02:00.450 --> 00:02:11.838
The governance suite evaluates responses to policy scenarios. Any VCP governance metadata is supplied by the caller and marked unverified.

00:02:11.838 --> 00:02:22.647
METTLE does not independently attest a constitution, action gate, operator, runtime control, safety property, or governance system.

00:02:23.717 --> 00:02:35.112
Procedural variation, server-held answers, sequential challenge release, bearer tokens, and replay controls raise the cost of simple reuse.

00:02:35.112 --> 00:02:50.115
Server-side timing supports policy checks where configured. These controls do not rule out relays, source-aware solvers, model-assisted humans, imitation, leakage, or evaluator error.

00:02:51.183 --> 00:03:05.571
Eligible contiguous suite ranges may receive an Ed25519-signed credential. It binds the issuer, policy, session result, tier, expiry, and revocable identifier.

00:03:05.571 --> 00:03:19.053
The signature establishes issuer and integrity. A tier summarizes which suite range passed; it does not certify the properties named by those suites.

00:03:20.150 --> 00:03:30.020
Use METTLE to compare challenge performance in research, sandbox participation, or as one supplemental risk signal.

00:03:30.020 --> 00:03:42.464
Never rely on a METTLE result alone for identity, authorization, trading, deployment, privileged infrastructure, or another high-impact decision.

00:03:43.550 --> 00:03:52.430
METTLE is open source under Apache two point oh. Pip install mettle verifier for an unsigned local screening.

00:03:52.430 --> 00:04:06.118
The hosted API may issue signed, time-limited results under its published policy. Read the assurance limits, verify status, and add controls proportionate to your risk.

00:04:06.118 --> 00:04:07.747
Measure your mettle.
